# The pinned Node base image for the root Dockerfile — single source of truth, same contract as
# tools/skopeo/pin.env and tools/cosign/pin.env: `tools/ci-mirror/images.list` REFERENCES these
# variables (never re-types the digest), `scripts/ci-mirror.sh` sources this file, and
# `deploy/airgap/src/skopeo-bin.test.ts`'s census asserts the Dockerfile's `ARG NODE_IMAGE=`
# default equals NODE_PINNED_IMAGE, so the three cannot drift apart.
#
# WHY THE BASE IMAGE IS PINNED BY DIGEST AT ALL (2026-08-31): `FROM node:22-trixie-slim` was the
# last un-pinned, un-mirrored third-party image on the E2E path — every compose build resolved the
# floating tag against Docker Hub LIVE, the exact dependency class that took CI red twice
# (quay.io timeout 2026-07-25; deleted digest 2026-08-18). A tag is not an identity.
#
# UPDATING: resolve the new index digest (`docker buildx imagetools inspect node:<tag>` or the
# registry API), update BOTH variables if the tag changes, and let CI job 4d re-mirror on the next
# run. The digest below is the multi-arch INDEX digest; job 4d mirrors the amd64 manifest it
# resolves to (see images.list's CAVEAT).
NODE_PINNED_VERSION=22-trixie-slim
NODE_PINNED_IMAGE=docker.io/library/node@sha256:7b8a0c89c54499bee567618f96578e1a12a800f062fbdbfd1fb6a443fa6f6284
